(a) It shall be unlawful for any person to commit an act of disorderly conduct in the city.
(b) A person commits disorderly conduct when he:
(1) Acts in a violent or tumultuous manner toward another person whereby that person is placed in fear of safety of his life, limb or health;
(2) Acts in a violent or tumultuous manner toward another person whereby the property of that person is placed in danger of being destroyed or damaged;
(3) Without provocation, uses to or of another person, in his presence, opprobrious or abusive words which by their very utterance tend to incite to an immediate breach of the peace; that is to say, words which as a matter of common knowledge and under ordinary circumstances will, when used to or of another person in his presence, naturally tend to provoke violent resentment, that is, words commonly called "fighting words";
(4) Without provocation, uses obscene and vulgar or profane language in the presence of or by telephone to a person under the age of 14 years, which threatens an immediate breach of the peace;
(5) Causes, provokes or engages in any fight, brawl or riotous conduct so as to endanger the life, limb, health or property of another;
(6) Disturbs the peace of others by violent, indecent, offensive or boisterous conduct or language which conduct or language was calculated to cause anguish or injury to another and had a direct tendency to cause immediate acts of violence by the person to whom the conduct or language was addressed, i.e., constituted "fighting words";
(7) Throws any stone or other missile upon or at any person, vehicle, building, tree, sign or other public or private property;
(8) Throws any stone or missile from any vehicle, either moving, stopped, or parked, upon or at any person, building, vehicle, tree, sign, or other public or private property;
(9) By acts of violence, interferes with another's pursuit of a lawful occupation;
(10) Expectorates, urinates, or defecates on any public street, alley, sidewalk or floor of any public building or a building where the public gathers or has access;
(11) With the intent to prevent or disrupt a lawful meeting, procession or gathering, substantially obstructs or interferes with the meeting, procession or gathering by physical action or verbal utterance;
(12) Frequents any public place with intent to obtain money from other persons by illegal and fraudulent schemes, tricks, artifices or devices; or
(13) Assembles for the purpose of engaging in any fraudulent scheme, device or trick to obtain any valuable thing in any place or from any person in the city, or who shall aid and abet therein.
(c) Any person who shall violate any subsection of this section may be charged with the offense of disorderly conduct, and on conviction thereof, shall be punished as provided in section 1-1-8.
(Code 1958, § 14-6; Code 1991, § 3-5-4; Ord. No. 2016-13, § I, 7-5-2016)
State Law reference— Assault and battery, O.C.G.A. § 16-5-20 et seq.; fraud and related offenses, O.C.G.A. § 16-9-50 et seq.; offenses against public order, O.C.G.A. § 16-11-30 et seq.; fighting in a public place, O.C.G.A. § 16-11-32; loitering or prowling, O.C.G.A. § 16-11-36; use of fighting words, obscene and vulgar or profane language, harassing telephone calls, O.C.G.A. §§ 16-11-39, 46-5-21; pointing or aiming gun or pistol at another, O.C.G.A. § 16-11-102.

